'''bearbine, bearbind''' (bēr′bīn, -bīnd), ''n.'' [< ''bear''<sup>3</sup> + ''bine'', ''bind'': see ''bine''<sup>1</sup>.] The name in England of several common species of ''Convolvulus'', as ''C. arvensis'', ''C. sepium'', and ''C. Soldanella'', from their twining about and binding together the stalks of barley. Also incorrectly written ''barebind.''
